NUM-31: spread routed outfall volume over the runoff step it is applied in

runoff_execute() passed the PREVIOUS runoff step to runoff_getOutfallRunon(),
which turns the volume an outfall routed onto a subcatchment into a rate,
vRouted / tStep. The rate is then applied over the CURRENT runoff step, which
has already been chosen and can be much longer (WET_STEP -> DRY_STEP) or
shorter, while the mass balance books vRouted. The subcatchment therefore
received vRouted x newStep / oldStep. Pass the current step instead; the
pollutant load is converted the same way.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-31_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/runoff.c b/src/legacy/engine/runoff.c
index bf00bad..608619a 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/runoff.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/runoff.c
@@ -244,7 +244,9 @@ void runoff_execute()
     for (j = 0; j < Nobjects[SUBCATCH]; j++) subcatch_setOldState(j);
 
     // --- determine any runon from drainage system outfall nodes
-    if ( oldRunoffStep > 0.0 ) runoff_getOutfallRunon(oldRunoffStep);
+    //     (the volume routed since the last runoff time is applied
+    //     over the runoff step about to be taken)
+    if ( oldRunoffStep > 0.0 ) runoff_getOutfallRunon(runoffStep);
 
     // --- determine runon from upstream subcatchments, and implement snow removal
     for (j = 0; j < Nobjects[SUBCATCH]; j++)
@@ -497,7 +499,7 @@ void  runoff_readFromFile(void)
 
 void runoff_getOutfallRunon(double tStep)
 //
-//  Input:   tStep = previous runoff time step (sec)
+//  Input:   tStep = current runoff time step (sec)
 //  Output:  none
 //  Purpose: adds flow and pollutant loads leaving drainage system outfalls
 //           during the previous runoff time step to designated subcatchments.
